<description>&lt;p&gt;Communal clashes have intensified in Lakes state, prompting a curfew and a visit by caretaker governor Rin Tueny, while UNMISS has increased civilian protection after deadly attacks in Rumbek. SSPDF soldiers were wounded in an assault on a Mundri West military outpost and the U.S. Embassy condemned an assault on WFP workers in Jonglei that involved looting of aid. An AIC cleric was shot dead in Juba and a Juba High Court sentenced five officers to 24 years for raiding a general's home. SPLA-IO forces retook Akobo after a deadly dawn clash. The lethal communal violence now far exceeds the two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMinAFBVV95cUxOM0YtNEVQN1RvMDA3R2NJR3JtV2ZvVGpZR3dZWHhEdFpDS29rOTBXU1hhdWp1alVHSFJlcHpYNlhqOElJVTlGT0pwRE9jdndScEp5a1pwUDNmaXcwcnlYVWpxb1VKOFh1VFFpbFoxYnRsa3R5VkhVa1pwV0JDV1NYY0xvUmpCNU1nSWxQYkNMQTdCM2Q4Zm5qSjVmVXE?oc=5&quot;&gt;ReliefWeb&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUEFVX3lxTE5xby1TOGhtdldEQ0hsQUNnemJidHU2QVhUX21ZSlFfNzQ2dnA5RnZTOWVzbl9UejdCWG5MWkpTWUt3ZEVZc0RkWXpfRmQwbEhw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudan Tribune&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMimAFBVV95cUxNUlRtbUtzaWc4TF9FUzJkaVB2UDdKWnlJcndoWW1FNEhBV215YWhLNENmRFFpeDFQak9OR2ZDeURnbnc2Vkh5VFY5YzA5TWNsZVFZZTJQbFZJMnVEd0pjM09MS0ItUERyZEhTSHVTY1RQdnNranVCWGtZZS1rU3Z3WU1zelU2YXk4RUt3QzNvZEM2d3BmWF9LMQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudans Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiowFBVV95cUxPcTVJaXl4WXU0V0RIaENrQ1YyVkQyQVlHQVVObS1ENjFaWUFRWWN5QVlVRm5fN0pWWHVWcEFCQktidXI5V3hpMS1uTmZxbUNzNFN4OFhILXBpaWdmVHFqOVctY1hWekd4NFoyVmVNU0p4VndrVG4za2Z3REZvTzh3QXF6ckM4UjluRjRxYTM1cTRJelF0cnBOS3JWT3UtR3YyR0lj?oc=5&quot;&gt;Radio Tam